1
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:24,650
This card

2
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:26,560
is your final card.

3
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:31,980
The Wheel of Fortune?

4
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:04,530
Now that we’re by the sea,

5
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:05,630
do you know how to...

6
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:08,030
ride the waves?

7
00:02:08,310 --> 00:02:09,620
Ride the waves?

8
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:11,500
What does that mean?

9
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:15,320
That spell somehow brought me here.

10
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:17,280
If you perform it again,

11
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:19,120
I might be able to return home, right?

12
00:02:19,910 --> 00:02:22,300
The English weapons trade records.

13
00:02:24,190 --> 00:02:24,800
Stop!

14
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:27,770
What happened to P’Khun?

15
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:28,560
Dech was shot

16
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,790
while searching for evidence against Okya-Wichayen.

17
00:02:30,790 --> 00:02:33,000
Our English weapons trade records

18
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:34,890
are missing.

19
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:57,500
It’s been almost a year

20
00:02:58,500 --> 00:02:59,720
since the day

21
00:03:00,730 --> 00:03:03,000
you were first admitted,

22
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:05,370
I’ve been hoping

23
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:08,390
you’d wake up and talk to me.

24
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,100
But as the days went by…

25
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:17,829
Grandma.

26
00:03:22,170 --> 00:03:22,950
Hello, Grandma.

27
00:03:22,950 --> 00:03:23,520
Hello, dear.

28
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,140
So is there any hope?

29
00:03:26,970 --> 00:03:29,260
I spoke to his doctor.

30
00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:31,850
There’s nothing to worry about.

31
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:33,990
His heart is normal.

32
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:35,420
His blood pressure is stable.

33
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:36,810
His muscles are in good shape

34
00:03:36,810 --> 00:03:39,440
because the therapist keeps working on them.

35
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:41,500
We just …

36
00:03:42,270 --> 00:03:45,310
don’t know when he’ll respond.

37
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:55,100
Great.

38
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:57,640
Are you dreaming?

39
00:03:58,329 --> 00:03:59,640
What are you dreaming about?

40
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:02,120
Can you open your eyes and talk to me?

41
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:04,200
Please wake up.

42
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:06,600
I miss you so much.

43
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:08,300
Great.

44
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,060
Wad.

45
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:42,950
Reung.

46
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:46,350
Why did you come to my house?

47
00:04:46,850 --> 00:04:48,310
Why can’t I?

48
00:04:50,130 --> 00:04:51,740
Is there something I should be afraid of?

49
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,950
I found the herb you were looking for,

50
00:04:57,950 --> 00:04:59,900
so I brought it to you.

51
00:05:01,330 --> 00:05:02,320
Agarwood?

52
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:03,740
That’s right.

53
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:11,740
Thank you, Reung.

54
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,250
Put it inside.

55
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:19,660
Yes.

56
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:30,730
Are you sure

57
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:33,540
you only came to give me the agarwood?

58
00:05:34,730 --> 00:05:36,310
Not because…

59
00:05:37,370 --> 00:05:38,240
I missed you.

60
00:05:53,610 --> 00:05:54,440
Reung.

61
00:05:56,630 --> 00:05:58,880
You know full well that you and I

62
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:02,270
can’t choose that path.

63
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:07,110
I’ve always believed

64
00:06:08,050 --> 00:06:09,190
that fate

65
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:11,730
is something we can’t change.

66
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,950
If there really is a next life,

67
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:22,470
I hope we get to choose our own path.

68
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:34,380
Love the right person,

69
00:06:34,950 --> 00:06:35,800
Reung.

70
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:47,300
Wad!

71
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:48,600
Reung!

72
00:07:08,850 --> 00:07:09,620
So

73
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:13,870
you never had eyes for another woman

74
00:07:15,130 --> 00:07:16,320
because of Reung?

75
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:18,830
Isn't that right?

76
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:26,410
I know that

77
00:07:27,190 --> 00:07:28,410
people’s hearts

78
00:07:29,670 --> 00:07:33,180
cannot be controlled as we wish.

79
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:36,730
But keep this in mind.

80
00:07:37,170 --> 00:07:40,770
Once you step out of this house,

81
00:07:42,350 --> 00:07:43,470
even I,

82
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:46,310
Okya-Kosathibodi,

83
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:49,150
cannot force anyone

84
00:07:50,190 --> 00:07:53,450
to accept a relationship...

85
00:07:57,220 --> 00:07:59,420
that goes against propriety.

86
00:08:02,230 --> 00:08:03,840
Don’t you agree, Reung?

87
00:08:05,740 --> 00:08:07,270
Yes, my lord.

88
00:08:13,050 --> 00:08:14,590
Even though

89
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:18,300
I know that,

90
00:08:18,860 --> 00:08:22,370
I still can’t deny my feelings for Wad.

91
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:32,900
I only ask that you understand

92
00:08:33,179 --> 00:08:34,419
and do not object.

93
00:08:36,110 --> 00:08:37,570
I promise

94
00:08:38,450 --> 00:08:40,110
I will never do anything

95
00:08:40,110 --> 00:08:41,960
to bring shame upon our family.

96
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:46,370
Reung and I

97
00:08:48,630 --> 00:08:51,100
will keep our feelings

98
00:08:51,850 --> 00:08:53,760
a secret.

99
00:10:03,450 --> 00:10:06,030
Did something happen?

100
00:10:08,550 --> 00:10:11,000
Dech and Gaew’s fortunes are troubling.

101
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:13,930
When they were young,

102
00:10:15,050 --> 00:10:16,560
I tied their fates,

103
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:20,880
hoping they would never have to part.

104
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:23,690
But now,

105
00:10:24,730 --> 00:10:26,780
the thread I tied

106
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,800
may have to unravel.

107
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:32,590
Good heavens.

108
00:10:33,910 --> 00:10:35,950
Is there anything you can do?

109
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,390
Why did you call me here?

110
00:10:39,390 --> 00:10:41,070
Are you going to perform a ritual?

111
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:45,380
Yes, a ritual to bring you good fortune.

112
00:10:49,290 --> 00:10:50,780
You know,

113
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:53,750
no one can defy fate.

114
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:55,820
I know.

115
00:10:56,620 --> 00:10:58,820
This will buy us some time,

116
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:02,590
so misfortune won’t come too soon.

117
00:11:11,330 --> 00:11:12,210
Put your palms together.

118
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:28,820
Here is your tea.

119
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:42,460
Is there anything you want?

120
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:46,380
Well…

121
00:12:51,970 --> 00:12:53,610
I wouldn’t say it’s good,

122
00:12:53,610 --> 00:12:55,040
but it’s not bad either.

123
00:13:01,350 --> 00:13:03,720
What's your opinion?

124
00:13:08,990 --> 00:13:12,620
You want to go back to where you came from, don’t you?

125
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:20,020
I came here

126
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:22,720
because of the Krishna Kali spell, right?

127
00:13:27,590 --> 00:13:30,920
Could you teach me that spell?

128
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:43,120
I miss home.

129
00:13:44,830 --> 00:13:46,320
I miss the people back there.

130
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,650
I miss Grandma.

131
00:14:02,850 --> 00:14:04,060
You can think of this place

132
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:08,050
as your home.

133
00:14:36,030 --> 00:14:39,880
Gaew wants to learn the Krishna Kali spell?

134
00:15:27,750 --> 00:15:28,420
Oh.

135
00:15:29,170 --> 00:15:30,720
Are you here to read too?

136
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,200
Looks like we’re on the same page.

137
00:15:53,570 --> 00:15:54,460
Let’s go, P’Yam.

138
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:55,920
Hey.

139
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:57,720
Where are you going?

140
00:15:58,330 --> 00:15:59,260
To the vej.

141
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:02,920
I’m going too.

142
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:03,840
Come on, Pin.

143
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,440
Yes, sir.

144
00:16:04,440 --> 00:16:06,060
Why do you suddenly need to go too?

145
00:16:06,060 --> 00:16:07,280
There’s only one bathroom.

146
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:08,940
Exactly.

147
00:16:09,730 --> 00:16:10,830
You go first.

148
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:12,080
I can wait.

149
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:15,430
Actually, I don’t need to go anymore.

150
00:16:15,700 --> 00:16:16,830
Forget it, Pin.

151
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:18,440
Yes, sir.

152
00:16:18,910 --> 00:16:20,280
What’s gotten into you?

153
00:16:21,830 --> 00:16:23,200
You go first.

154
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:24,970
Let’s go, P’Yam.

155
00:16:25,530 --> 00:16:26,160
Yes, sir.

156
00:16:26,160 --> 00:16:27,060
Let’s go, Pin.

157
00:16:32,810 --> 00:16:33,900
I’m not going anymore.

158
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,180
You go first.

159
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:36,790
You should go first.

160
00:16:37,310 --> 00:16:38,640
I’ll wait outside.

161
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:40,400
I don’t want to go anymore.

162
00:16:43,150 --> 00:16:44,610
I don’t really want to go either.

163
00:17:05,579 --> 00:17:06,410
Gaew!

164
00:17:06,670 --> 00:17:08,520
Why do you keep following me?

165
00:17:08,730 --> 00:17:09,589
Gaew.

166
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:11,280
I told you…

167
00:17:11,839 --> 00:17:13,790
I won’t let you out of my sight.

168
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:15,430
I’m not a kid.

169
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:17,770
You don’t have to follow me everywhere.

170
00:17:18,060 --> 00:17:18,880
I feel uncomfortable.

171
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:22,839
You feel uncomfortable?

172
00:17:23,319 --> 00:17:24,839
Yes, I do.

173
00:17:50,810 --> 00:17:51,720
Gaew.

174
00:17:53,070 --> 00:17:53,980
Are you asleep yet?

175
00:18:00,410 --> 00:18:02,310
He’s been asleep for a while,

176
00:18:02,310 --> 00:18:04,200
and he doesn’t want anyone disturbing him.

177
00:18:05,030 --> 00:18:05,920
But…

178
00:18:07,670 --> 00:18:09,150
I just saw the light on.

179
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:11,220
He’s asleep now, sir.

180
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,900
Where are you going?

181
00:18:29,980 --> 00:18:31,530
Don’t follow me.

182
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:34,430
I want to be alone.

183
00:18:35,950 --> 00:18:36,680
Yes, sir.

184
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:51,570
Why are you angry with Lord Khun?

185
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:53,110
P’Yam.

186
00:18:53,890 --> 00:18:54,640
Yes?

187
00:18:55,350 --> 00:18:56,830
If you knew that one day

188
00:18:56,830 --> 00:18:58,460
you’d have to leave

189
00:18:59,270 --> 00:19:00,990
and never see me again,

190
00:19:02,330 --> 00:19:03,970
before that day,

191
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,090
whenever it may come,

192
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:10,420
would you keep serving me as always,

193
00:19:11,410 --> 00:19:14,400
or teach me how to live on my own

194
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:15,590
when you’re no longer here?

195
00:19:17,410 --> 00:19:20,730
Is that why you’ve been avoiding him?

196
00:19:23,210 --> 00:19:25,660
Isn’t that too cruel?

197
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:28,960
Am I really that cruel?

198
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:32,650
We’ll suffer when it’s time to part,

199
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:34,550
so why suffer now

200
00:19:34,550 --> 00:19:36,070
when we miss each other?

201
00:19:36,910 --> 00:19:38,100
So,

202
00:19:38,770 --> 00:19:41,200
please don’t let yourself suffer

203
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:42,820
just because you’ll have to be apart.

204
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:45,710
I think

205
00:19:46,150 --> 00:19:47,740
Lord Khun is hurting.

206
00:19:58,320 --> 00:19:59,040
P’Yam.

207
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:15,200
Where are you sleeping tonight, you fool?

208
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:17,680
I’m sleeping with you, idiot.

209
00:20:29,270 --> 00:20:29,910
Pin.

210
00:20:30,530 --> 00:20:32,280
I told you I wanted to be alone.

211
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:36,650
Don’t you understand?

212
00:20:40,010 --> 00:20:40,920
Gaew.

213
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:45,970
I’m sorry

214
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:49,260
for ignoring you.

215
00:20:53,310 --> 00:20:54,400
All this time,

216
00:20:55,790 --> 00:20:57,320
I kept thinking

217
00:20:58,100 --> 00:20:59,340
that if I wasn’t here,

218
00:21:00,910 --> 00:21:02,300
you wouldn’t be able to go on.

219
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:08,450
Is that why you keep your distance from me?

220
00:21:11,720 --> 00:21:12,780
I thought...

221
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:16,030
if I slowly distanced myself from you

222
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:21,330
until the day we have to part,

223
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:39,980
then when that day comes,

224
00:21:42,150 --> 00:21:43,320
I’d be heartbroken.

225
00:21:44,850 --> 00:21:46,020
I’d miss you.

226
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,730
But it hasn’t come yet.

227
00:21:52,390 --> 00:21:53,510
And today,

228
00:21:55,150 --> 00:21:56,850
you’re still right here,

229
00:21:59,790 --> 00:22:01,160
so I won’t do anything

230
00:22:02,480 --> 00:22:05,880
that we’ll regret

231
00:22:07,020 --> 00:22:08,410
or suffer for.

232
00:22:12,390 --> 00:22:13,200
Gaew.

233
00:22:19,330 --> 00:22:20,700
Thank you

234
00:22:23,410 --> 00:22:24,750
for being kind to me.

235
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,630
Do you know?

236
00:22:33,470 --> 00:22:35,170
Just thinking about…

237
00:22:36,060 --> 00:22:37,940
not having you by my side

238
00:22:39,430 --> 00:22:40,590
already hurts.

239
00:22:43,020 --> 00:22:44,820
But having you right here

240
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:47,740
and being unable to get close

241
00:22:48,940 --> 00:22:50,460
is even more painful.

242
00:23:05,650 --> 00:23:07,090
I promise you,

243
00:23:09,820 --> 00:23:11,400
if one day

244
00:23:14,790 --> 00:23:16,870
you aren’t here anymore,

245
00:23:21,460 --> 00:23:22,620
wherever you are,

246
00:23:23,940 --> 00:23:25,420
I'll find you

247
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:29,900
and love you.

248
00:24:34,540 --> 00:24:36,090
Okya-Wichayen.

249
00:24:38,350 --> 00:24:39,970
Lord Muen nearly died because of him.

250
00:24:40,840 --> 00:24:43,300
Why hasn’t anyone held him accountable?

251
00:24:45,100 --> 00:24:47,140
Because no one dares to.

252
00:24:47,660 --> 00:24:49,560
That’s why he can still walk around

253
00:24:49,840 --> 00:24:51,390
like he’s done nothing wrong.

254
00:24:52,220 --> 00:24:54,550
If we can’t bring him to justice,

255
00:24:55,100 --> 00:24:56,190
then we’ll have to kill him.

256
00:24:59,340 --> 00:25:00,190
You’re right.

257
00:25:01,660 --> 00:25:02,900
If we can’t take him to justice,

258
00:25:04,990 --> 00:25:06,280
we’ll have to take his life.

259
00:25:10,540 --> 00:25:11,670
Follow me, Yam.

260
00:25:27,500 --> 00:25:28,590
Huh?

261
00:25:28,590 --> 00:25:29,850
Isn’t this liquor?

262
00:25:30,660 --> 00:25:32,110
What liquor?

263
00:25:32,300 --> 00:25:33,370
This is oil.

264
00:25:34,390 --> 00:25:35,420
Whoa.

265
00:25:36,790 --> 00:25:38,970
Are you sure about this?

266
00:25:39,470 --> 00:25:40,630
I’m sure.

267
00:25:41,860 --> 00:25:42,920
Now’s our chance.

268
00:25:43,370 --> 00:25:44,300
There’s no one around.

269
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:46,140
Go.

270
00:25:56,580 --> 00:25:57,190
Here.

271
00:26:18,250 --> 00:26:19,740
The building is on fire, my lord!

272
00:26:19,740 --> 00:26:20,540
Hurry and go see!

273
00:26:24,170 --> 00:26:26,890
Those are Khun Sriwisanwaja’s servants.

274
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:30,080
Follow me.

275
00:26:38,230 --> 00:26:39,620
Let’s hurry home, Gaew.

276
00:26:39,980 --> 00:26:41,150
It’s going to rain.

277
00:26:41,410 --> 00:26:42,160
Alright.

278
00:26:43,510 --> 00:26:47,030
You’re sightseeing as if it’s your last.

279
00:27:17,350 --> 00:27:18,070
Hey!

280
00:27:27,660 --> 00:27:28,380
Hey!

281
00:27:33,290 --> 00:27:34,050
You!

282
00:27:40,890 --> 00:27:43,150
Okkhun-Sriwisanwaja.

283
00:29:05,540 --> 00:29:06,490
P’Khun.

284
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:09,810
P’Khun!

285
00:30:09,120 --> 00:30:09,990
Gaew!

286
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:11,510
Gaew!

287
00:30:12,460 --> 00:30:14,080
Go search everywhere.

288
00:30:14,080 --> 00:30:14,890
Yes, sir.

289
00:30:16,500 --> 00:30:17,430
Gaew.

290
00:30:18,380 --> 00:30:19,420
Gaew!

291
00:30:21,020 --> 00:30:22,050
Gaew!

292
00:30:23,700 --> 00:30:24,910
Gaew!

293
00:31:35,370 --> 00:31:36,640
Ever since he woke up,

294
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:38,890
he’s been spacing out.

295
00:31:38,890 --> 00:31:40,770
Is something wrong with his brain?

296
00:31:42,220 --> 00:31:45,590
We’ve examined him thoroughly,

297
00:31:46,740 --> 00:31:48,640
but everything is normal.

298
00:32:12,380 --> 00:32:13,500
He’s here.

299
00:32:14,930 --> 00:32:16,930
Dech, are you hungry?

300
00:32:28,290 --> 00:32:31,050
I feel so sorry for him.

301
00:32:33,940 --> 00:32:36,310
Nothing can ease this kind of suffering

302
00:32:37,440 --> 00:32:38,610
except time.

303
00:32:41,820 --> 00:32:44,580
But time can be so cruel.

304
00:33:07,680 --> 00:33:10,040
Shall I bring your food?

305
00:33:12,200 --> 00:33:13,040
Leave.

306
00:33:15,980 --> 00:33:16,640
Yes, sir.

307
00:33:42,030 --> 00:33:43,760
I miss you so much,

308
00:33:44,120 --> 00:33:44,960
Gaew.

309
00:34:03,470 --> 00:34:04,940
They all look so good.

310
00:34:05,610 --> 00:34:06,530
Okay.

311
00:34:07,500 --> 00:34:08,699
Wait, Grandma.

312
00:34:13,960 --> 00:34:14,880
Here you go.

313
00:34:16,070 --> 00:34:17,070
Whoa.

314
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:21,900
Why did you make crispy catfish salad today?

315
00:34:21,900 --> 00:34:23,360
And fruit salad too.

316
00:34:23,360 --> 00:34:25,480
Everything is so sour.

317
00:34:30,460 --> 00:34:31,889
Enjoy your meal.

318
00:34:31,889 --> 00:34:32,820
Alright.

319
00:34:39,219 --> 00:34:39,960
Delicious.

320
00:34:40,949 --> 00:34:41,850
Really delicious.

321
00:34:46,420 --> 00:34:48,699
Why do you always space out?

322
00:34:49,420 --> 00:34:51,090
Is something bothering you?

323
00:34:52,770 --> 00:34:54,690
I miss P’Khun.

324
00:34:57,290 --> 00:35:00,020
It’s normal to miss a fictional character.

325
00:35:00,490 --> 00:35:02,680
What’s the name of this novel?

326
00:35:04,250 --> 00:35:05,680
I’d like to read it.

327
00:35:06,460 --> 00:35:08,910
It’s even set in the Ayutthaya period,

328
00:35:09,200 --> 00:35:09,840
huh?

329
00:35:10,180 --> 00:35:11,630
Ever since I woke up,

330
00:35:12,380 --> 00:35:13,740
I’ve been confused

331
00:35:14,170 --> 00:35:15,490
about what’s real and what isn’t.

332
00:35:18,340 --> 00:35:20,190
You were unconscious for a long time.

333
00:35:20,500 --> 00:35:23,310
You may have dreamed about many things,

334
00:35:23,790 --> 00:35:25,550
so take your time.

335
00:35:26,060 --> 00:35:27,940
If something is bothering you,

336
00:35:27,940 --> 00:35:30,170
you can talk to me.

337
00:35:30,170 --> 00:35:31,520
We’ll figure it out together.

338
00:35:32,830 --> 00:35:34,900
Then tonight,

339
00:35:34,900 --> 00:35:37,680
come sleep here and tell me the story again.

340
00:35:38,060 --> 00:35:39,840
I’m still wondering

341
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:42,510
when Dech fell for Gaew.

342
00:35:43,350 --> 00:35:44,350
It’s really delicious.

343
00:36:02,270 --> 00:36:02,900
Oh.

344
00:36:12,950 --> 00:36:14,640
Looks like it’s pretty serious.

345
00:36:58,540 --> 00:36:59,500
Gaew,

346
00:37:04,040 --> 00:37:05,660
Wherever you are,

347
00:37:07,200 --> 00:37:09,400
I’ll find you

348
00:37:11,650 --> 00:37:12,890
and love you.

349
00:39:28,570 --> 00:39:31,990
Khun Sriwisarnwaja,

350
00:39:33,940 --> 00:39:34,830
Dech,

351
00:39:36,020 --> 00:39:37,760
and his friend,

352
00:39:39,220 --> 00:39:40,240
Gaew.

353
00:39:57,030 --> 00:39:58,070
Gaew.

354
00:39:59,390 --> 00:40:00,480
P’Khun?

355
00:40:01,880 --> 00:40:03,060
Are you all right?

356
00:40:05,490 --> 00:40:06,550
I’m fine.

357
00:40:09,230 --> 00:40:10,160
Sorry.

358
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:23,620
I really did go there.

359
00:40:24,670 --> 00:40:27,450
(Residence of Okya-Horathibodi)

360
00:40:42,720 --> 00:40:44,940
He has been like this for quite some time.

361
00:40:45,960 --> 00:40:47,090
I’m afraid

362
00:40:48,720 --> 00:40:51,040
he’ll pine away and fall ill.

363
00:40:53,470 --> 00:40:54,730
Do you still remember

364
00:40:55,570 --> 00:40:57,620
when Lord Gaew came here?

365
00:40:58,560 --> 00:41:00,640
He didn’t come here by ordinary means.

366
00:41:03,930 --> 00:41:05,160
It was because of

367
00:41:07,670 --> 00:41:09,210
the Krishna Kali spell!

368
00:41:13,760 --> 00:41:15,290
You said that

369
00:41:16,600 --> 00:41:18,290
I appeared here

370
00:41:18,850 --> 00:41:21,640
after you performed the Krishna Kali spell.

371
00:41:23,250 --> 00:41:24,410
I think

372
00:41:25,700 --> 00:41:28,170
that spell somehow brought me here.

373
00:41:32,670 --> 00:41:34,470
Krishna Kali spell.

374
00:41:41,710 --> 00:41:42,750
My lord!

375
00:41:43,700 --> 00:41:44,680
My lord!

376
00:42:16,250 --> 00:42:18,120
-Call the surgeon immediately.
-Yes, Doctor.

377
00:42:21,130 --> 00:42:23,590
Patient is bleeding into his abdominal cavity.

378
00:42:24,100 --> 00:42:25,650
Drain the blood as fast as you can.

379
00:42:25,650 --> 00:42:26,760
Prepare the anesthesia.

380
00:42:26,760 --> 00:42:28,040
We’re operating now.

381
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:51,640
Doctor, his blood pressure is dropping!

382
00:44:48,900 --> 00:44:50,920
Do you… know who I am?

383
00:44:54,480 --> 00:44:55,540
I do.

384
00:44:59,400 --> 00:45:01,410
You’re my attending physician.

385
00:45:03,830 --> 00:45:05,140
I mean…

386
00:45:06,400 --> 00:45:07,830
have we met before?

387
00:45:10,420 --> 00:45:11,380
Yes.

388
00:45:19,520 --> 00:45:20,670
Yesterday,

389
00:45:20,670 --> 00:45:21,790
the day before,

390
00:45:22,370 --> 00:45:23,400
and today.

391
00:45:24,660 --> 00:45:26,190
Pretty much every day.

392
00:45:34,820 --> 00:45:35,930
No,

393
00:45:36,870 --> 00:45:38,410
I mean…

394
00:45:39,480 --> 00:45:40,890
Are you okay?

395
00:45:51,170 --> 00:45:52,470
I won’t be around for a few days.

396
00:45:53,030 --> 00:45:55,070
Just stay for another day or two,

397
00:45:55,070 --> 00:45:56,370
then you can go home.

398
00:45:57,690 --> 00:45:58,420
Got it.

399
00:46:10,600 --> 00:46:11,600
That’s great.

400
00:46:12,210 --> 00:46:13,830
With all this rest,

401
00:46:13,830 --> 00:46:15,000
you’ll recover quickly.

402
00:46:19,290 --> 00:46:20,400
I’m leaving now.

403
00:46:40,790 --> 00:46:43,520
(One week later.)

404
00:46:46,290 --> 00:46:47,360
Did you call for me?

405
00:46:47,620 --> 00:46:48,600
Come on in.

406
00:46:50,660 --> 00:46:53,040
I’d like to introduce you to our new doctor.

407
00:46:53,040 --> 00:46:56,040
He’s a top-tier surgeon from the US.

408
00:46:57,070 --> 00:46:58,100
A new doctor?

409
00:47:10,160 --> 00:47:11,280
You?

410
00:47:15,220 --> 00:47:16,920
This is Dr. Duncan.

411
00:47:17,280 --> 00:47:20,920
He joined us while you were unconscious.

412
00:47:22,840 --> 00:47:25,140
Nice to meet you, Dr. Great.

413
00:47:57,640 --> 00:47:58,560
Nice to meet you too.

414
00:48:00,400 --> 00:48:02,360
I feel so lucky

415
00:48:02,360 --> 00:48:06,580
to have two top surgeons at our hospital.

416
00:48:06,580 --> 00:48:08,720
So I have to decide

417
00:48:08,720 --> 00:48:12,520
who will be the new head of the surgery department.

418
00:48:20,480 --> 00:48:22,920
Even though Dr. Duncan is a top surgeon,

419
00:48:23,220 --> 00:48:24,750
he’s also my patient.

420
00:48:25,850 --> 00:48:28,080
Shouldn’t we let him recover first?

421
00:48:29,950 --> 00:48:31,080
Are you fully recovered?

422
00:48:31,970 --> 00:48:32,970
Yes.

423
00:48:33,570 --> 00:48:35,030
I’m ready to work.

424
00:48:36,500 --> 00:48:38,030
Do you want to test me?

425
00:48:40,740 --> 00:48:42,480
And don’t you know...

426
00:48:42,740 --> 00:48:44,810
that while you were unconscious for almost a year,

427
00:48:45,400 --> 00:48:47,200
I was the doctor

428
00:48:48,040 --> 00:48:48,970
who took care of you?

429
00:49:02,960 --> 00:49:04,760
Overall, his condition is stable.

430
00:49:04,760 --> 00:49:06,500
His blood pressure and pulse are normal.

431
00:49:07,000 --> 00:49:08,870
But we still can’t determine

432
00:49:08,870 --> 00:49:10,550
why he hasn’t regained consciousness.

433
00:49:13,220 --> 00:49:14,260
It may be

434
00:49:15,010 --> 00:49:16,430
acute shock.

435
00:49:21,310 --> 00:49:23,470
Are you fully recovered, then?

436
00:49:24,990 --> 00:49:26,580
I accept your challenge.

437
00:49:27,050 --> 00:49:28,080
Let’s put it to the test.

438
00:49:29,590 --> 00:49:32,240
Between the two of you,

439
00:49:32,240 --> 00:49:34,710
whoever performs better

440
00:49:34,710 --> 00:49:39,140
will become the new head of the surgery department.

441
00:49:39,700 --> 00:49:40,550
-Deal.
-Deal.

442
00:52:16,100 --> 00:52:16,820
Hello, Great.

443
00:52:16,820 --> 00:52:17,950
Are you coming tonight?

444
00:52:19,180 --> 00:52:20,540
I’m not sure.

445
00:52:20,540 --> 00:52:22,880
This 16-hour case really exhausted me.

446
00:52:23,340 --> 00:52:24,740
Come on, just show up.

447
00:52:24,740 --> 00:52:26,460
Everyone’s already here.

448
00:52:27,380 --> 00:52:29,580
I just want to go home to my grandma, Rich.

449
00:52:30,220 --> 00:52:31,980
It doesn't happen often.

450
00:52:31,980 --> 00:52:32,860
Tell you what.

451
00:52:32,860 --> 00:52:34,260
Drinks are on me tonight.

452
00:52:38,010 --> 00:52:39,020
Fine, fine.

453
00:52:39,800 --> 00:52:40,760
I'll be there.

454
00:52:54,840 --> 00:52:55,970
Hello?

455
00:52:57,220 --> 00:52:58,340
Huh?

456
00:52:59,100 --> 00:53:00,300
The parking lot?

457
00:53:00,860 --> 00:53:01,940
Okay, okay.

458
00:53:03,780 --> 00:53:04,500
What move is that?

459
00:53:04,500 --> 00:53:06,500
I'm stepping out for a sec.

460
00:53:06,500 --> 00:53:08,100
Okay.

461
00:53:08,100 --> 00:53:08,820
Hurry back.

462
00:53:08,820 --> 00:53:09,460
Sure thing.

463
00:53:15,180 --> 00:53:17,380
Why’d you call me out here?

464
00:53:18,100 --> 00:53:19,180
Uh...

465
00:53:19,980 --> 00:53:22,020
My phone got locked. Can you take a look for me?

466
00:53:22,460 --> 00:53:23,820
It’s locked?

467
00:53:23,820 --> 00:53:25,300
Then how did you call me?

468
00:53:26,980 --> 00:53:29,180
I don’t know. It suddenly locked.

469
00:53:32,740 --> 00:53:33,740
Hey.

470
00:53:34,220 --> 00:53:35,340
What are you doing?

471
00:53:35,340 --> 00:53:36,780
Face scan.

472
00:53:38,460 --> 00:53:40,140
Look at the camera.

473
00:53:41,780 --> 00:53:43,180
Tilt your head down a bit.

474
00:53:46,460 --> 00:53:47,980
It must’ve fixed itself.

475
00:54:00,380 --> 00:54:01,940
Wanna hang out with me?

476
00:54:02,860 --> 00:54:04,740
Where are you taking me, Big Bro?

477
00:54:05,620 --> 00:54:06,820
You’ll see.

478
00:54:08,140 --> 00:54:09,340
Get in.

479
00:54:10,500 --> 00:54:11,220
Wait,

480
00:54:11,220 --> 00:54:12,860
I need to go that side.

481
00:54:12,860 --> 00:54:13,820
Oh, right.

482
00:54:14,340 --> 00:54:15,420
Over there.

483
00:54:29,780 --> 00:54:31,140
Ah!

484
00:54:33,820 --> 00:54:34,900
Hey!

485
00:54:36,300 --> 00:54:37,780
Dr. Duncan!

486
00:54:38,340 --> 00:54:39,860
So you're here.

487
00:54:40,700 --> 00:54:42,140
You.

488
00:54:42,140 --> 00:54:44,220
What’s your problem with me?

489
00:54:44,940 --> 00:54:46,860
Why are you acting so cold and distant?

490
00:54:48,780 --> 00:54:50,140
Okay.

491
00:54:50,780 --> 00:54:51,900
You…

492
00:54:52,700 --> 00:54:54,260
saved my life

493
00:54:55,020 --> 00:54:56,900
when I was unconscious.

494
00:54:57,980 --> 00:54:59,420
But I…

495
00:55:00,380 --> 00:55:02,140
saved yours too

496
00:55:03,140 --> 00:55:05,330
when you were in a coma.

497
00:55:15,860 --> 00:55:17,100
What do you want?

498
00:55:17,620 --> 00:55:19,140
I…

499
00:55:19,140 --> 00:55:21,380
don't want anything from you.

500
00:55:22,460 --> 00:55:23,820
I…

501
00:55:23,820 --> 00:55:25,740
never wanted to compete with you.

502
00:55:26,820 --> 00:55:28,020
If you...

503
00:55:28,700 --> 00:55:30,380
want it that badly,

504
00:55:31,060 --> 00:55:32,900
then just take it!

505
00:55:35,100 --> 00:55:36,700
But why...

506
00:55:38,420 --> 00:55:41,180
do you have to mess with my feelings?

507
00:55:44,180 --> 00:55:46,340
Why the hell do you look like–
